resolution: "Git text merging remains SDK-owned with protected tracker overrides and v2 compatibility. Native acceptance now pins fixture core.autocrlf and checks exact LF and CRLF disjoint outcomes, preserving overlapping and binary conflict controls."
expected_result: "Native disjoint edits combine under both configured LF and CRLF policies while conflicting text retains markers, binary bytes and stages remain intact, and tracker merge rules remain structured."
actual_result: "All11 native merge/fence cases and the linked test pass after the fixture correction. Both explicitly configured core.autocrlf=false (LF) and true (CRLF) disjoint cases assert exact native worktree bytes and both edits; standard overlapping markers, raw binary bytes and three conflict stages remain strict. Uncached ESLint with an empty suppression file passes. No production source, package API, workflow, coverage denominator or threshold changed from9abfaee, whose complete local static gate and10,407-case suite pass at exact100% coverage. The failed Windows annotation and failed full-review request are retained as distinct receipts; prior78a86 review does not approve9abfaee. The corrected head must receive renewed required checks and bot review before merge."
