body: "Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1460\n\n## Problem\n`pm merge install` writes this into the tracked `.gitattributes` fence:\n```gitattributes\n\".agents/pm/**/*.json\" merge=pm-json\n\".agents/pm/extensions/**\" -merge\n\".agents/pm/extensions/.managed-extensions.json\" merge=pm-json\n```\nThe source comment (`src/sdk/merge/install.ts`, added in #916) says the intent is an escape hatch: extension package assets should not go through the pm item and stream drivers. But `-merge` does not mean \"no custom driver\". In gitattributes, **`-merge` (unset) means \"treat as binary\"**:\n- when both branches change an extension file, Git keeps the current branch's version as the tentative result and reports a conflict;\n- it writes **no conflict markers**, so the other side's edit can easily be lost, because the file looks clean;\n- non-conflicting edits from both sides are not combined either.\n\nWhat the comment describes is `!merge` (unspecified, meaning Git's built-in 3-way text merge) or an explicit `merge=text`. Either one excludes the files from `pm-json` / `pm-relationship` without making them binary.\n\n## Impact\nAny repository that vendors or develops an extension under `.agents/pm/extensions/` (fleet packages do this during development and in packed-consumer tests) gets binary-merge semantics on text sources. A code-review bot flagged it on a downstream PR (unbraind/pm-lint#6). Consumers cannot fix it locally: the fence is generated, and `pm health` reports any edit as `merge_fence_drift`.\n\n## Proposal\n1. Emit `\".agents/pm/extensions/**\" merge=text` (or `!merge`) instead of `-merge`, and keep the later `merge=pm-json` override for `.managed-extensions.json`.\n2. Bump the fence version marker so `pm merge install` / health refresh existing fences.\n3. Add a test that merges two branches each editing a different line of an extension source file: expect a clean text merge. Editing the same line should produce standard conflict markers.\n\n\nImplementation intent\n\nCorrect generated extension asset merge semantics without sending package content to tracker drivers or selecting binary merge for text sources."
